---
import Card from '../../design-system/components/Card.astro';
import Cluster from '../../design-system/composition/Cluster.astro';
import Section from '../../design-system/composition/Section.astro';
import Button from '../../design-system/primitives/Button.astro';
import FaqItem from '../../design-system/patterns/FaqItem.astro';
import FaqList from '../../design-system/patterns/FaqList.astro';
import PageHero from '../../design-system/patterns/PageHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const questions = [
  [
    'Can Jethos move assets that remain in my wallet?',
    'Jethos does not automatically invest or move unrelated wallet assets. Movement requires a valid wallet signature or a token approval you have granted. You remain responsible for keys, signatures and reviewing/revoking approvals.',
  ],
  [
    'Does “under my control” mean absolute immunity?',
    'No system can make that absolute promise. It means Jethos cannot move assets you have not deposited or separately approved. Anyone who controls your keys, a contract with an existing allowance, token-issuer controls or a vulnerability may still affect assets. Self-custody replaces intermediary custody with explicit ownership and responsibility.',
  ],
  [
    'What changes after I deposit?',
    'The selected base asset moves into the vault system and you receive shares representing the position. From that point, the capital follows deployed contract logic, configured integrations and documented administrative controls.',
  ],
  [
    'Who controls a Jethos vault?',
    'User ownership is represented through shares and withdrawal rights under the contract rules. Strategy execution and administrative functions use roles described in the technical documentation. The PoC is curated and not currently governed as a permissionless public system.',
  ],
  [
    'Is Jethos a bank?',
    'No. “Self-custodial financial home” describes the intended user experience. Jethos is currently DeFi software and a private proof of concept, not a regulated bank or insured deposit provider.',
  ],
  [
    'Are returns or principal guaranteed?',
    'No. Smart contracts, protocols, assets, oracles, markets and operational systems can fail. Jethos aims to make constraints and evidence understandable, not to remove risk.',
  ],
  [
    'Can I always withdraw immediately?',
    'Not necessarily. The PoC currently uses a synchronous withdrawal path, but liquidity, reserve rules, pauses and protocol conditions can cause a transaction to fail or require unwinding. Future products may explicitly show immediate, unwinding or pending states.',
  ],
  [
    'Is the complete Jethos system audited?',
    'The site does not claim a completed independent audit of the whole Jethos system. Underlying protocol audits cover their respective systems, not every Jethos integration and control.',
  ],
  [
    'Why does the App request a USDC approval?',
    'USDC is an ERC-20 token. LiquidityManager needs an allowance before it can transfer the exact amount selected for deposit. The App requests an exact approval rather than an unlimited one.',
  ],
  [
    'Can I revoke the approval?',
    'Yes. The PoC console includes a revoke action that sets the LiquidityManager USDC allowance to zero. Revoking does not withdraw an existing vault position.',
  ],
  [
    'What is live today?',
    'A private Arbitrum USDC proof-of-concept deployment and its recorded Aave, Euler and Morpho integrations. The broader wallet, multi-profile, multi-asset and financial-services experience remains progressive development or vision.',
  ],
  [
    'What problem does Jethos solve?',
    'Jethos aims to combine a familiar financial interface with self-custodial ownership, understandable vault choices and verifiable capital routes. The current PoC validates only a narrow foundation of that direction.',
  ],
  [
    'Who is Jethos designed for?',
    'The intended product is for people who want a simpler way to hold, invest and understand digital assets without hiding the technical and financial risks. The current deployment is for controlled technical validation, not general consumers.',
  ],
  [
    'Why begin with native USDC on Arbitrum?',
    'A single native stablecoin and an established EVM network reduce the first validation scope. USDC still has issuer and depeg risk; Arbitrum still has smart-contract, sequencer and network dependencies.',
  ],
  [
    'How does Jethos choose protocols?',
    'The target methodology considers expected return together with liquidity, maturity, utilization, concentration and risk limits. Final numeric Conservative policy limits remain decisions to publish; registration alone does not imply allocation.',
  ],
  [
    'What fees can Jethos charge?',
    'The PoC contracts expose configured deposit and withdrawal fee reads. The console shows the current result when available. Future management, performance or service fees require explicit product policy and disclosure.',
  ],
  [
    'What does Conservative mean today?',
    'For the current PoC it means a native-USDC, supply-only validation scope. Reserve, concentration, utilization, oracle and stress thresholds are not presented as final until policy decisions are approved.',
  ],
  [
    'What if the frontend is unavailable?',
    'On-chain contracts do not depend on this specific webpage to exist, but direct interaction requires correct addresses, ABI knowledge and careful transaction construction. The deployment record and developer documentation are intended to support verification; recovery procedures remain an assurance gate.',
  ],
  [
    'Who controls administrative roles?',
    'The code contains parameter, emergency and upgrade-related components, but the current public evidence pack does not yet publish a complete role map, owner addresses, multisig or timelock evidence. This remains explicitly open in the Trust Center.',
  ],
  [
    'Will payments, cards or credit make Jethos a bank?',
    'No such capability is live. Any future payments, cards, credit or regulated asset service would require suitable technical and regulated partners, legal analysis and precise disclosures. The phrase financial home describes the intended experience, not a banking licence.',
  ],
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Jethos FAQ — Wallet control, vaults and the PoC"
  description="Clear answers about wallet ownership, vault transparency, approvals, withdrawals, risks and the current Jethos proof of concept."
  page="faq"
  canonicalPath="/pages/faq.html"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Frequently asked questions"
    title="Control, choice and transparency."
    description="The short answers to what Jethos can access, what changes inside a vault and what is actually available today."
  />
  <Section narrow
    ><FaqList
      >{
        questions.map(([question, answer], index) => (
          <FaqItem {question} open={index === 0}>
            {answer}
          </FaqItem>
        ))
      }</FaqList
    ></Section
  >
  <Section compact
    ><Card variant="accent" class="split"
      ><div>
        <h2>Want the implementation details?</h2><p>
          Review protocol architecture, risk assumptions, trust boundaries and live PoC reads.
        </p>
      </div><Cluster
        ><Button href="/app.html">Open PoC</Button><Button
          href="/pages/trust-center.html"
          variant="secondary">Trust Center</Button
        ><Button href="/pages/docs.html" variant="ghost">Docs</Button></Cluster
      ></Card
    ></Section
  >
</BaseLayout>
